WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.792 --> 00:00:16.354
stepped out of the cart and climbed up the steep path from Dorfli, carrying her basket.

2
00:00:17.974 --> 00:00:22.476
The baker had promised to send her suitcase up to Grandfather's the next day.

3
00:00:24.197 --> 00:00:29.839
She recognized every tree along the way, and the high tops of the mountains looked down on her

4
00:00:29.919 --> 00:00:31.080
like old friends.

5
00:00:32.572 --> 00:00:37.235
At last, Heidi caught sight of the hut where Peter and his grandmother lived.

6
00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:43.059
With her heart beating louder and louder, she ran up to the door and burst in.

7
00:00:43.079 --> 00:00:45.841
"Oh my!"

8
00:00:46.482 --> 00:00:47.923
cried a voice from the corner.

9
00:00:47.943 --> 00:00:52.145
"That was just how Heidi used to run in.

10
00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:54.187
Who is there?"

11
00:00:54.647 --> 00:00:55.348
asked Grannie.

12
00:00:56.168 --> 00:00:57.509
"It is I, Grannie!"

13
00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:01.732
cried Heidi, and she ran and flung her arms around her.

14
00:01:02.764 --> 00:01:05.466
Grannie was so surprised that she couldn't speak.

15
00:01:06.967 --> 00:01:15.211
She stroked Heidi's head quietly and said at last, "Yes, yes, that is Heidi's hair and her voice.

16
00:01:16.432 --> 00:01:17.833
It really is you.

17
00:01:18.453 --> 00:01:19.494
Thank God."

18
00:01:20.535 --> 00:01:23.176
Tears of joy fell from the blind woman's eyes.

19
00:01:23.196 --> 00:01:29.460
"Yes, Grannie, it's really me," answered Heidi.

20
00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:33.919
"I have come back and I am never going away again.

21
00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.723
And you won't have any more hard bread to eat.

22
00:01:38.183 --> 00:01:44.609
Look!" One by one, Heidi took out the white rolls and piled them on Grannie's lap.

23
00:01:44.629 --> 00:01:48.753
"What a present to bring me!"

24
00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:52.316
exclaimed Grannie as her hands touched the soft bread.

25
00:01:52.336 --> 00:01:56.360
"But you're the best present of all!"

26
00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:02.226
"I was afraid you might have died while I was gone," cried Heidi.

27
00:02:02.246 --> 00:02:05.327
"And you would never get to taste the rolls."

28
00:02:06.748 --> 00:02:09.069
Grannie smiled and stroked Heidi's cheeks.

29
00:02:10.209 --> 00:02:16.972
After a friendly pause, Heidi reached into her basket, pulled out her old straw hat, and put it

30
00:02:17.152 --> 00:02:23.735
on. She told Grannie she had to go home to Grandfather, but promised to visit the next day.

31
00:02:25.535 --> 00:02:29.377
On her way up the steep path, Heidi paused to look all around her.

32
00:02:30.518 --> 00:02:35.142
The beauty of the mountain with the rocks aglow in the sun was just as she remembered.

33
00:02:36.162 --> 00:02:41.966
She dropped her basket, threw her arms above her head, and hopped from foot to foot with pure

34
00:02:42.046 --> 00:02:47.110
joy. Then she picked up her basket and started to run.

35
00:02:48.211 --> 00:02:55.056
First she saw the tops of the fir trees, then the roof of Grandfather's hut, and at last,

36
00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.522
Grandfather sitting in his favorite seat.

37
00:02:58.582 --> 00:03:01.765
"Grandfather, Grandfather," she called.

38
00:03:02.685 --> 00:03:07.028
She ran up, jumped onto his lap, and clasped her arms about his neck.

39
00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:16.315
For the first time in years, Grandfather's eyes were moist with tears, and he had to brush them

40
00:03:16.395 --> 00:03:17.315
away with his hand.

41
00:03:17.335 --> 00:03:21.759
"So you have come back to me, Heidi," he said.

42
00:03:21.779 --> 00:03:23.560
"Why is that?

43
00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:25.425
Did they send you away?"

44
00:03:25.445 --> 00:03:28.446
"Oh no, Grandfather.

45
00:03:28.866 --> 00:03:30.927
Don't think that," said Heidi.

46
00:03:30.947 --> 00:03:36.349
"They were all so kind, Clara, her father, and Grandmamma.

47
00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:39.391
But I was very homesick.

48
00:03:40.371 --> 00:03:43.833
I used to get a lump in my throat as if I were choking.

49
00:03:44.613 --> 00:03:48.354
I never said anything because I didn't want to be ungrateful.

50
00:03:49.895 --> 00:03:54.661
And then, suddenly, one morning Clara's father said I could come home.

51
00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:58.143
I'm sure the letter explains it all."

52
00:03:59.223 --> 00:04:02.745
She hopped down and handed him the packet and letter from her basket.

53
00:04:03.625 --> 00:04:06.306
Then hand in hand, they went inside.

54
00:04:06.326 --> 00:04:13.729
"The packet is for you," said Grandfather after reading the letter.

55
00:04:13.749 --> 00:04:15.870
"Put it in the cupboard.

56
00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:20.272
It is money for you to buy a bed and any clothes you may need.

57
00:04:21.264 --> 00:04:24.886
And now, Heidi, do you think you can still drink milk with me?"

58
00:04:25.807 --> 00:04:26.327
he asked.

59
00:04:27.708 --> 00:04:29.770
Eagerly Heidi sat down on her stool.

60
00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:34.252
Grandfather filled her cup right to the brim and handed it to her.

61
00:04:35.393 --> 00:04:37.494
Holding it with two hands, Heidi drank.

62
00:04:37.514 --> 00:04:45.760
"Our milk tastes nicer than anything else in the world, Grandfather," she said and smiled.
